  "language_contract": "compiler-dev/1",
  "notes": [
    "Identity is (allocation address, per-address generation); legal address reuse must not overwrite earlier history.",
    "Collector metadata allocations are raw blocks: they are reported and must be freed by exit in the current runtime, but are excluded from Vec payload bytes and from live-Vec free ordering.",
    "Pressure target follows development/plans/MEMORY_INTEGRATION.md: initial 128 successful registrations, then max(128, 2*live) budget, handled at stable function/loop heads, with a normal single-thread main-return final collection. It is an implementation choice, not a source scope/marker guarantee.",
    "The 2 MiB payload budget counts Vec payload bytes (allocation size minus the runtime Vec header) for live Vec generations only. RSS, page cache and raw metadata bytes are not used.",
    "The small cycle fixtures may be reclaimed by the normal final collection; no eager per-scope collection is required."
  ],
